      "readme": "Spinal cord fMRI activity with electrocutaneous stimulation \n\n\nData includes:\n\n- Anatomical defaced T2w spinal cord image\n- Functional spinal cord data for 3 runs of ~9min of electrocutaneaous stimulation of the right middle finger at 4 individualized stimulation intensities.\n\n\tIn derivatives/labels:\t\n\t- Anatomical T2w spinal cord image\n\t- Warping field for anatomical to PAM50 template based on rootlets registration\n\t- Anatomical T2w spinal nerve root labels \n\t- Anatomical T2w intervertebral disc labels \n\t- Motion corrected functional images for each run\n\t- Segmentation of spinal cord and canal of functional images\n\t- Warping field for functional to PAM50 template registration\n\t- Task vectors (fsl_stim_vectors)\n\t- Processed physio files \n\n\nNote: plase cite the following paper if you use this dataset: Bédard, S., et al. (2026). Spatial distribution of spinal cord fMRI activity with electrocutaneous stimulation. Imaging Neuroscience\n\n",
